Thanks for comment. Yes missed that one. Now I've looked a bit more and thought about removing whole referenceid map since there is no insertion to this map anymore. But I saw referenceid mapping is used in gtpv2 dissector then hesitate a bit.

If i understand it correctly, works like that.

- Referenceid mapping is inserted from dissectnotifyuri.
- gtpv2 lookup referenceid mapping if there is any imsi with this teid (teid = referenceid)

So since this change remove whole insertion to referenceid map then lookup from gtpv2 would always fail. But I don't know how to replace it. Notifyuri would not match with teid since it is whole path. Maybe do lookup from location map? 

Related code from packet-gtpv2.c:

```c
else if (gtpv2_hdr->message == GTPV2_MODIFY_BEARER_REQUEST) {
                    /* If MBEAREQ and not already in the list then we create a new session*/
                    add_gtp_session(pinfo->num, gtp_session_count);

                    if (args->imsi) {
                        imsi = wmem_strdup(wmem_file_scope(), args->imsi);
                        wmem_map_insert(session_imsi, GUINT_TO_POINTER(gtp_session_count++), imsi);
                    } else {
                        /* If handover from 5G, look up referenceid from earlier HTTP2 streams */
                        static char to_str_back_buf[32];
                        #define BACK_PTR (&to_str_back_buf[31]) /* pointer to NUL string terminator */

                        char* referenceid = uint_to_str_back(BACK_PTR, (uint32_t)gtpv2_hdr->teid);
                        imsi = http2_get_imsi_from_referenceid(referenceid);
                        if(imsi) {
                            wmem_map_insert(session_imsi, GUINT_TO_POINTER(gtp_session_count++), imsi);
                        }
                    }
```

Yeah, that would be a miss. Possible change would be

```
    if (http2_3gpp_session) {
        char *imsi = NULL;
        if(stream_info->imsi && (strcmp(stream_info->imsi, "") != 0)) {
            add_assoc_imsi_item(tvb, http2_tree, stream_info->imsi);
        } else if (stream_info->referenceid && (strcmp(stream_info->referenceid, "") != 0) && (imsi = http2_get_imsi_from_location(stream_info->referenceid))) {
            add_assoc_imsi_item(tvb, http2_tree, imsi);
        } else if (stream_info->path && (strcmp(stream_info->path, "") != 0) && (imsi = http2_get_imsi_from_notifyuri(stream_info->path))) {
            add_assoc_imsi_item(tvb, http2_tree, imsi);
        }
    }
```

would be better if follow the pattern as above

```
    else if (stream_info->path && (strcmp(stream_info->path, "") != 0)){
        imsi = http2_get_imsi_from_notifyuri(stream_info->path);
    }
```

Right! okej, but change to
```
if (!imsi && stream_info->path && (strcmp(stream_info->path, "") != 0)){
        imsi = http2_get_imsi_from_notifyuri(stream_info->path);
    }

```

